{"name":"Hat Box Brown","hex":"#8f775d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hat","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Haitian Creole."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A covering for the head, often in the approximate form of a cone, dome or  cylinder closed at its top end, and sometimes having a brim and other decoration.","A particular role or capacity that a person might fill."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hat"},{"term":"box","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Buamu."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Senses relating to a three-dimensional object or space.\n A cuboid space; a cuboid container, often with a hinged lid.","A cuboid space; a cuboid container, often with a hinged lid."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/box"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Box Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brian \"Box\" Brown is an American cartoonist whose first work was the online comic Bellen!\nHe was awarded in 2011 a Xeric Grant for the comic Love is a Peculiar Type of Thing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Brown%2C_Box_-MBFI.jpg/330px-Brown%2C_Box_-MBFI.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Box_Brown","wikidata":"Q4951487"},{"title":"Hat box","blocks":[{"text":"A hat box is a container for storing and transporting headgear, protecting it from damage and dust. A more generic term for a box used to carry garments, including headgear, is a bandbox. Typically, a hat box is deep and round in shape, although it may also be boxlike and used 